WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:07.009
You edge the poolside, chlorine-stenched air
filling your nose, the sounds of splashing

00:00:07.009 --> 00:00:12.070
and lifeguards whistling bouncing off the
indoor pool facility walls.

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:18.260
The water ripples, family and friends egging
you to cannonball in, the pool almost beckoning

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:20.949
you to jump with its suggestive waves.

00:00:20.949 --> 00:00:28.230
Yet there remains an underlying fear, one
that brings your hands to your face and causes

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:35.770
your teeth to chatter, even as the pool, clear
as glass with chlorine, hides no secrets.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:43.260
A monster, some teeth-gnashing megalodon ascending
from the depths of extinction; leviathan curling

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:49.960
its barbed tail to strike its prey at any
moment; or even some vast, unknowable force,

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:56.820
ancient as Earth, hardly comprehensible to
human minds, waiting, dreaming to breach the

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:57.820
surface.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:05.940
No matter what form this gargantuan, invisible
monster takes, you know one thing: once you

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:09.150
jump in, you will not return to shore.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:13.760
You take a moment, recompose yourself, and
laugh off the fear.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:18.650
Maybe a product of too much research on the
Bloop, that deep-ocean sound continuing to

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:25.010
confound scientists as to its cause, or maybe
too much binging Infographics videos on sea

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:30.830
monsters, krakens and Loch Ness Monsters,
mysterious globsters cast onto shores throughout

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:32.440
America.

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:38.110
Whatever the origin, the thought seems ridiculous
to you now, and your fears regarding invisible

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:46.370
sharks stalking the pool perimeter escape
your mind as you hurl yourself into the water.

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:50.210
SCP-1128
In the vast archives of a hidden site, stuffed

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:56.159
into a drawer amongst uncountable horrors
like it, the SCP Foundation holds a description

00:01:56.159 --> 00:02:02.500
of a vast, unfathomable horror, that'll make
you more suspicious the next time you pass

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:07.180
a pool, lake, or even a bathtub or puddle
of water.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:13.840
SCP-1128 is a gigantic aquatic monster, lurking
in waters unknown, and that's all the Foundation

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:17.280
will let anyone not assigned to testing know
about it.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:21.250
While the Foundation has never shied away
from those Moby Dicks of the deep, including

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:27.819
the several-thousand kilometer-long arthropod
SCP-169, and has even utilized such predators

00:02:27.819 --> 00:02:36.500
in the past for their own benefit, like the
lengthy beast SCP-3000, SCP-1128 poses a unique

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:42.560
challenge: anyone who knows of its description
beyond surface-level details will fall under

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.550
the anomaly's effect.

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:50.460
The representation you see now is merely an
artist's interpretation of the basic prompt.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:54.950
The Foundation, of course, had to discover
the monster's effects in the first place.

00:02:54.950 --> 00:03:00.020
The chain of communication becomes foggy,
but a tip from an unknown source alerted the

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:04.980
Foundation to the monster's existence, and
details regarding its manifestation.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:10.150
One man, who had stumbled upon the entity's
full description, started developing acute

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:13.750
thalassophobia, the fear of large bodies of
water.

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:15.700
Not bodies in the water, mind you.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:21.160
The man refused to relax on the beach or fly
overseas, claiming he could see the monster's

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:25.590
dark silhouette lurking underwater, ever scouting
for him.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:31.900
This eventually extended to even closed bodies
of water, like lakes, ponds, and pools, still

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:36.819
insisting that the creature swam under the
surface, trailing him wherever he went.

00:03:36.819 --> 00:03:41.930
His friends dismissed him as crazy, and he
too believed he had fallen under some hysteria.

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:48.150
He decided to take a nice, warm bath to soothe
his mind and ease his troubles.

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:50.920
He turned on the faucet, and let the tub fill
up.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:56.190
He put on his best bathing suit ready to calm
his anxiety once and for all.

00:03:56.190 --> 00:04:01.530
This had been plaguing his mind for far too
long and he was ready to rid all the negativity

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:03.650
surrounding this phobia.

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:08.890
Basically he was sick and tired of being sick
and tired over the idea of it all.

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:14.860
He mustered up the courage and with the anticipation
to just simply relax, he took his first confident

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:16.470
step into the tub.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:20.529
He paused for a moment and breathed a sigh
of relief.

00:04:20.529 --> 00:04:24.270
He picked up his other foot and stepped fully
into the bath.

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:25.270
SPLASH!

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:27.659
He fell straight down right through the tub.

00:04:27.659 --> 00:04:32.259
Waves and bubbles blocked his vision, his
arms flailed as he sunk deeper into an abyss

00:04:32.259 --> 00:04:33.740
of water and fear.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.439
This wasn’t supposed to happen, he thought.

00:04:36.439 --> 00:04:41.069
Several moments later, while still in a full
on panic, the buoyancy of his body began to

00:04:41.069 --> 00:04:46.289
slow his sinking.The bubbles from his underwater
screams rose above him, and he began to follow

00:04:46.289 --> 00:04:49.979
their direction, scrambling back up to where
he'd come.

00:04:49.979 --> 00:04:54.240
Just as he made it back to the surface of
the tub water - choking and hyper-ventilating

00:04:54.240 --> 00:05:00.330
in terror - he swore he could see a distant
creature, the very same that stalked him through

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:03.999
oceans and pools, staring at him.

00:05:03.999 --> 00:05:08.330
Shaking, he hoisted himself out of the water,
and ran out of the house.

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:12.469
Hysterical, he ran through the surrounding
neighborhood, desperately searching for someone

00:05:12.469 --> 00:05:14.969
he could relay his experience to.

00:05:14.969 --> 00:05:18.870
Blinded by fear, he neglected to spot a puddle
in the middle of the road he ran on.

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:24.469
He raised his foot, arched forward, and landed
straight into the seemingly shallow water.

00:05:24.469 --> 00:05:25.469
SPLASH!

00:05:25.469 --> 00:05:29.219
Again, he found himself completely submerged
and drowning.

00:05:29.219 --> 00:05:34.379
After a minute, he did emerge from the puddle,
but not in one piece.

00:05:34.379 --> 00:05:38.249
Knowledgeable of this incident,
the Foundation set about expunging any traces

00:05:38.249 --> 00:05:42.460
of the monster's description from the world,
physical and digital.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:46.479
The description had low distribution according
to the results of Foundation web crawlers,

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:49.289
but this hardly stopped the Foundation's endeavor.

00:05:49.289 --> 00:05:54.949
With forum posts deleted, individuals located
and amnesticized, and catalogs trawled to

00:05:54.949 --> 00:06:00.660
ensure the description did not proliferate,
the Foundation engaged in what it does best:

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:03.169
Questionably ethical experiments.

00:06:03.169 --> 00:06:09.379
First, they had an anonymous D-Class, uninformed
of the creature's effect, read the description

00:06:09.379 --> 00:06:10.379
of the beast.

00:06:10.379 --> 00:06:14.589
While the pamphlet they gave him confused
him somewhat, he didn't feel particularly

00:06:14.589 --> 00:06:19.889
frightened by the entity, and he confusedly
put on the diving suit the Foundation testers

00:06:19.889 --> 00:06:21.150
provided him.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:26.430
As they connected him to a cable and told
him to enter a bathtub, the D-Class did as

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:27.979
they instructed him.

00:06:27.979 --> 00:06:32.909
The D-Class expressed initial confusion at
the tub's depth, remarking that it "looked

00:06:32.909 --> 00:06:34.900
so tiny from the outside''.

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:40.499
As the D-Class continued to descend, he analyzed
his surroundings, realizing the nautical reality

00:06:40.499 --> 00:06:41.639
that enveloped him.

00:06:41.639 --> 00:06:47.819
He asked how an ocean got stuffed into a bathtub,
but the test organizer had no room for miscellaneous

00:06:47.819 --> 00:06:48.819
talk.

00:06:48.819 --> 00:06:54.639
He continued to descend until he hit the sandy
bottom, seaweed covering the ocean floor.

00:06:54.639 --> 00:06:56.499
The D-Class looked around.

00:06:56.499 --> 00:07:02.659
Tropical fish swam in schools, coral covered
the seabed, and to his right dropped an immense

00:07:02.659 --> 00:07:05.479
cliff, a sheer edge.

00:07:05.479 --> 00:07:10.940
The test organizer advised the D-Class to
approach the cliff, and he begrudgingly complied.

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:15.969
As he struggled in his diving suit, he fell
back and screamed.

00:07:15.969 --> 00:07:17.360
SCP-1128 The aquatic horror

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:23.650
swam distantly, gracefully even, and paid
no attention to the D-Class so fixated upon

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:24.650
it.

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:28.780
He realized that the creature matched the
one he read on the pamphlet, and almost complained

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:33.759
about this when he saw a blue whale swimming
alongside SCP-1128.

00:07:33.759 --> 00:07:37.289
Compared to the monster, the whale looked
like a guppy.

00:07:37.289 --> 00:07:40.750
The whale glided in front of SCP-1128's jaws.

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:47.599
The monster remained tranquil, stared at its
prey, and bit the whale in two with one chomp.

00:07:47.599 --> 00:07:49.980
Its teeth glistened in the water.

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:53.929
The test operator requested the D-Class to
pull back, and as the cable began to draw

00:07:53.929 --> 00:07:58.919
him toward where he came, the D-Class stared
at the creature, swallowing the chunks of

00:07:58.919 --> 00:08:00.240
whale whole.

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:05.979
The D-Class' eyes remained fixated on the
creature, partly in fright, partly in awe.

00:08:05.979 --> 00:08:10.759
He wondered how ocean trawlers hadn't discovered
such a giant beast yet, with the world effectively

00:08:10.759 --> 00:08:16.939
under one hundred percent surveillance - something
the D-Class knew far too well as a convict.

00:08:16.939 --> 00:08:23.610
Yet, the D-Class recognized - and if not comprehended
- partially understood the ocean's vastness

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:24.750
and mystery.

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:30.830
The dark depths reveal no inkling as to their
contents, and a creature like the giant squid

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:35.479
or the coelacanth
can remain in hiding for centuries, if not

00:08:35.479 --> 00:08:36.500
millennia.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:42.030
It held him in wondrous thought to consider
the vastness of the depths.

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:48.050
When SCP-1128 stopped and stared at the D-Class,
this feeling of wonder was quickly replaced

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:49.490
with fear.

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:54.180
As the creature approached, the D-Class pleaded
with the test operators for help, as the test

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:56.550
operators accelerated the rate of the cable
returning.

00:08:56.550 --> 00:09:01.970
The D-Class took short, shallow breaths, filling
his body with dangerous nitrogen as he ascended,

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:03.300
further impairing his judgment.

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:09.440
He had devolved to gibberish and screaming
when, face-to-face, the monster consumed its

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:10.440
prey.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:15.910
The cable went slack, and the test operator
pulled up only a broken wire, snapped, the

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:18.330
water turning a cloudy red.

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:23.350
The test operator knew that unprotected D-Class
had no chance at survival against the monster,

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:26.200
but he could potentially arm and shield them.

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:31.420
He had another, similarly ignorant D-Class
once again dress in a Scuba suit and enter

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:32.420
the tub.

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:37.980
However, the test operator placed the D-Class
within a shark cage, ala the movie Jaws, and

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:41.130
lowered the cage in with another cable and
winch system.

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:47.290
While unsure how this would fare with SCP-1128,
the test operator remained hopeful that the

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:49.630
D-Class could survive and recount his story.

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:54.200
Unfortunately, as the cage lowered into the
tub, the test operator received no response

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:59.971
from the D-Class until the line spontaneously
tightened, snapped, and loosened.

00:09:59.971 --> 00:10:04.500
Hoping to find the D-Class' remains, the test
operator only found shredded pieces of metal,

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:07.260
torn and twisted like taffy.

00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:11.840
The test operator decided that he could utilize
the Foundation's arsenal to his advantage,

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:17.300
and use an anomalously toughened shark cage
in his testing, perhaps using an anomaly like

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:20.540
the clockwork machine SCP-914.

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:24.950
He gained approval from his higher-ups to
undergo this procedure, and after some testing,

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:30.990
beheld a shining, strong-as-Titanium shark
cage, which he placed another D-Class within.

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:36.570
Hoping for a success with the monster, however,
proved unsatisfactory, as the same thing happened

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:40.970
as the previous test, only without any sort
of metallic remains.

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:46.450
While bitter that the monster had won again,
he wondered where the cage had landed.

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:52.420
Meanwhile, Foundation forces labored tirelessly
to find SCP-1128's location, hoping to avoid

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:54.520
any civilian contact with the creature.

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:59.940
Luckily, a GPS signal established itself upon
the most recent D-Class' test, with the tracking

00:10:59.940 --> 00:11:03.790
device on the D-Class signifying the monster's
general location.

00:11:03.790 --> 00:11:08.690
The Foundation has redacted the location of
the monster, perhaps in a vain attempt to

00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:12.430
hide a very near threat from potential readers.

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:17.530
The Foundation set up a team of only the most
talented boaters in its forces, Mobile Containment

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:20.260
Force Kappa-12, Sea Devils.

00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:25.800
Upon arriving at the location, the Sea Devils
discovered the previously enhanced shark cage,

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:27.200
completely undamaged.

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:32.290
However, closer inspection revealed traces
of human DNA on the bars, though the Foundation

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:36.650
could not confirm whether the DNA belonged
to the previously-sent D-Class.

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:41.790
The test operator, while glad his shark cage
survived the monster's attack, still found

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:44.490
himself dissatisfied with the overall results
of the test.

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:49.370
He knew he needed to quell this creature's
impact before a large population viewed it

00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:55.590
or knew of it, but the horrible beast had
evaded all attempts at peaceful interaction.

00:11:55.590 --> 00:11:59.640
Perhaps with a madness not unlike Captain
Ahab, yearning for the death of his white

00:11:59.640 --> 00:12:04.850
whale, the test operator armed a D-Class with
a specialized weapon, designed to deal with

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:06.700
aquatic threats promptly.

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:11.940
This weapon, potentially another of the Foundation's
precious arsenal, could potentially harm if

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:13.750
not kill the creature.

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:18.780
While he knew the Foundation's mission statement
forbade unnecessary destruction, the test

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:22.690
operator felt it may turn necessary if matters
turn any worse.

00:12:22.690 --> 00:12:29.090
Thus, he sent his armed D-Class through the
tub once more, ready to engage the beast in

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:30.090
combat.

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:33.300
The attempt, as one may expect, didn't last
long.

00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:37.630
The D-Class, upon spotting the creature, aimed
his weapon at the monster and attacked it,

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:43.010
but rather than drive the creature away, it
only turned intently upon the D-Class, as

00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:44.750
if desiring a fight.

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:50.070
The D-Class barely managed to scrape SCP-1128
before the creature devoured the D-Class,

00:12:50.070 --> 00:12:53.400
leaving the test operator once again empty-handed.

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:58.850
Defeated, and without any more resources to
deal with the beast, the test operator ceased

00:12:58.850 --> 00:13:04.850
his attempts at besting the creature and followed
the Foundation's more cautious approach, expunging

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:10.210
any publicly-found descriptions of SCP-1128
as needed and diverting any vessels away from

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:14.460
the anomaly's exclusion zone, as maintained
by the Sea Devils.

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:18.750
While the creature had proven treacherous
in unexpected situations prior, engulfing

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:23.580
the man who first heard the creature's description
in a rain puddle, researchers could hardly

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:25.820
expect what would transpire.

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:31.030
A D-Class, afflicted with the monster's effect
and observed for testing, avoided all bodies

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:32.410
of water as required.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:37.090
Eventually, however, the D-Class needed to
interact with some kind of water: drinking

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:38.130
water.

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:43.190
In a choice between a little water exposure
or certain death, the D-Class felt inclined

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:44.430
to choose the former.

00:13:44.430 --> 00:13:49.570
He filled his cup with water and, for fun,
placed his finger into the cup, dropping it

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:51.120
into the water.

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:56.960
SCP-1128, unseen from the outside, violently
pulled the D-Class through the cup into its

00:13:56.960 --> 00:13:58.500
watery domain.

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:01.790
The D-Class had not a chance to scream.

00:14:01.790 --> 00:14:06.170
This alarmed containment staff, now cognizant
that even the tiniest specs of water could

00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:11.120
transport an afflicted person into SCP-1128's
ocean territory.

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:16.910
This proved particularly strenuous when a
new report of a potential SCP-1128 manifestation

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:17.910
arose.

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:23.920
An old woman, isolated with her cats and knitting
supplies, found an article online with a description

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:25.370
of the monster.

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:29.660
Frightened and disgusted by what she had read,
she closed the article and continued on with

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:31.220
her monotonous life.

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:36.380
Such a life would take a turn for the worse,
however, when she too developed that all-encompassing

00:14:36.380 --> 00:14:37.740
water-based fear.

00:14:37.740 --> 00:14:43.270
Her apartment overlooked an outdoor pool,
and one day, looking outside, she swore she

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:49.279
could see that same dark silhouette as the
man did, lurking in the water among kids and

00:14:49.279 --> 00:14:50.730
parents playing.

00:14:50.730 --> 00:14:56.210
She swiftly closed the window curtains and
taped the seams shut, allowing no light to

00:14:56.210 --> 00:14:57.210
peek through.

00:14:57.210 --> 00:15:01.840
Eventually, this paranoia affected her hygiene,
neglecting showers and baths for fear of the

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:02.840
creature's wrath.

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:07.720
She swore she could see the silhouette in
any individual droplet of water.

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:13.040
Her skin began to flake as she avoided water
as much as humanly possible, cracks developing

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:17.770
on her arms, legs, and face, inflaming into
rashes and itches.

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:20.700
Her scratching further increased the flaking.

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:27.480
She even eliminated water from her diet, sealing
the faucets with duct tape and consuming exclusively

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:28.750
orange juice.

00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:31.380
She threw out her cats' water bowls, dehydrating
them.

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:36.520
They pleaded with her as she continued to
devolve, avoiding any contact with the outside

00:15:36.520 --> 00:15:40.400
world even as it attempted to contact her.

00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:44.990
Eventually, a concerned neighbor contacted
the local police concerning the situation,

00:15:44.990 --> 00:15:50.510
and the case caught the Foundation's radar,
recognizing the symptoms of a potential SCP-1128

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:51.680
infection.

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:55.810
A mobile task force disguised themselves as
civilians to enter the apartment building

00:15:55.810 --> 00:15:58.120
and potentially interfere with the woman's
condition.

00:15:58.120 --> 00:16:02.640
They entered the complex, climbing up the
stairs with barraging equipment for forced

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:06.960
entry, as would prove necessary to use to
enter the woman's apartment.

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:11.460
She had nailed the door shut with wood and
sealed the cracks along the sides with plaster,

00:16:11.460 --> 00:16:14.660
in an attempt to keep out any water vapor.

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:17.380
She had, similarly, blocked the window with
wood planks.

00:16:17.380 --> 00:16:23.550
A horrid miasma of dead skin and citrus filled
the apartment, the old woman soaking it in,

00:16:23.550 --> 00:16:25.700
ever avoiding the dreaded monster.

00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:30.070
The Foundation task force attempted peaceful
entry, knocking on the door and asking if

00:16:30.070 --> 00:16:31.980
anyone lived in the apartment.

00:16:31.980 --> 00:16:37.420
The woman couldn't speak if she wanted to;
her throat had dried to near silence save

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:38.420
a croak.

00:16:38.420 --> 00:16:42.830
Suddenly, the task force and the woman heard
a rumbling noise outside.

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:44.050
Thunder.

00:16:44.050 --> 00:16:45.279
Rain.

00:16:45.279 --> 00:16:48.592
The woman panicked, and yelped "Don't come
in here!"

00:16:48.592 --> 00:16:50.010
in a froggy voice.

00:16:50.010 --> 00:16:54.800
The task force eventually decided they needed
to use their equipment, and entered via barrage.

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:59.120
The door collapsed in as an immensely dense
air clogged the task force's sight, blinding

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:00.400
and choking them.

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:03.779
The woman shrieked, and backed against the
window inadvertently.

00:17:03.779 --> 00:17:08.880
The task force insisted they were here to
help the woman, but she simply heaved heavily,

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:13.139
saying something unintelligible in that dry,
cracking voice.

00:17:13.139 --> 00:17:19.639
The rain began pounding on the window, patter-patter-patter,
as the task force attempted to gain a hold

00:17:19.639 --> 00:17:20.639
on the woman.

00:17:20.639 --> 00:17:24.529
She resisted their movements, moving around
the room while the task force intentionally

00:17:24.529 --> 00:17:26.679
avoided violent confrontation.

00:17:26.679 --> 00:17:32.200
The rain grew in intensity as the woman continued
running around her apartment, tripping over

00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:33.630
her starved cats.

00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:37.980
Eventually, she fell back onto the window,
at which the boards blocking it fell onto

00:17:37.980 --> 00:17:40.690
the floor, exposing the pouring rain fully.

00:17:40.690 --> 00:17:48.159
She screamed, as she saw the silhouette of
the monster staring at her in every individual

00:17:48.159 --> 00:17:49.380
rain drop.

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:55.480
One drop landed on her skin, and she violently
vanished, pulled into a miniscule spec of

00:17:55.480 --> 00:17:56.480
water.

00:17:56.480 --> 00:18:00.700
The task force collapsed from exhaustion,
perhaps dreading their inevitable amnestic

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:04.210
treatment following exposure with an SCP-1128
afflictee.

00:18:04.210 --> 00:18:10.325
Yet, they couldn't help but wonder what the
old woman saw in a single spec of water that

00:18:10.325 --> 00:18:13.830
could cause that degree of fear and paranoia.

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:19.889
The kind of fear only caused by entire oceans,
condensed into a single droplet.

00:18:19.889 --> 00:18:24.990
Besides the monster, what else did she see
in those multitude of droplets?

00:18:24.990 --> 00:18:30.650
The fish that populated the sea, the whale
carcasses left behind by SCP-1128, the Sea

00:18:30.650 --> 00:18:35.309
Devils viewed from below, drifting on the
water, unsuspecting?

00:18:35.309 --> 00:18:41.860
Just as one may view a grain of sand and see
the Sahara, she too saw that rain drop and

00:18:41.860 --> 00:18:47.360
viewed an ocean entire, along with whatever
malevolent creatures inhabit it.

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:52.110
One may have more sympathy for the child,
reluctant to jump into the pool water, knowing

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:57.029
not necessarily that something inhabits that
body of water, but that the body belongs to

00:18:57.029 --> 00:19:03.460
a cycle much larger than itself, larger than
any sea or ocean, and the only thing that

00:19:03.460 --> 00:19:06.590
can traverse that cycle is a monster.

00:19:06.590 --> 00:19:10.740
A creature like SCP-1128.

00:19:10.740 --> 00:19:14.869
The task force went back to their local site
to report what happened during the incident.

00:19:14.869 --> 00:19:19.690
Like so many incidents the Foundation deals
with, the sum total of those that risk their

00:19:19.690 --> 00:19:25.700
lives for the greater good is a couple memory-erasing
syringes and another update to documentation.

00:19:25.700 --> 00:19:32.259
A description of SCP-1128 remains in a stuffy
locker, lurking in wait among other horrifying

00:19:32.259 --> 00:19:37.169
stories in the SCP database's sea of terror.

00:19:37.169 --> 00:19:41.150
Just like that test operator that attempted
to best the monster, could the Foundation's

00:19:41.150 --> 00:19:45.940
attempts ever surmount the possibility of
another person being afflicted?

00:19:45.940 --> 00:19:48.059
Could they conquer the sea?

00:19:48.059 --> 00:19:54.210
In a member of that task force's dreams, they
perceive a dark blue ocean, and the distant

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:57.110
black shadow that resides within.

00:19:57.110 --> 00:20:03.940
And from this ocean they can view the bath
tubs, sinks, pools, puddles, cups of water,

00:20:03.940 --> 00:20:08.590
and rain droplets of the world, seen from
below.

00:20:08.590 --> 00:20:15.379
Although they know not what SCP-1128 looks
like, they too experience the fear it summons

00:20:15.379 --> 00:20:19.750
among those that do, the paranoia, the fear.

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:26.440
Although it may not manifest directly in people's
lives, it can always be observed, stalking,

00:20:26.440 --> 00:20:27.440
waiting.

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:29.999
Lurking under a murky surface.

00:20:29.999 --> 00:20:33.490
Watching with hidden eyes.

00:20:33.490 --> 00:20:40.450
Now go check out “SCP-3000 - Anantashesha”
and “SCP-057-IT - Under the Sea” for more

00:20:40.450 --> 00:20:44.080
anomalous entities that lurk in the deep and
dark depths of the Sea!

